  "findings": [
    "Three executions of 100 turns end in the same game: the same final hash and the same trail of 100 turn hashes, whichever way the heavy panel is closed.",
    "The live heap at rest was flat to the byte once the game stopped changing (turn 14): 2,117,320 bytes with unmounting and 2,443,832 with hiding, growth 0 between the medians of the halves.",
    "The pause holds the accepted job at its first phase while the HUD answers; it does so only because the HUD's CanvasLayer is PROCESS_MODE_ALWAYS (the pause-kills-ui sabotage makes it pausable and the click never reaches the handler).",
    "Hiding a 100-node panel is not cheaper in CPU as a whole (the sum of the open and the close is inside the run-to-run noise), has a shorter tail on the open, a slower close, and keeps 100 nodes and 326,512 bytes of heap.",
    "The host updates all 101 nodes of a hidden panel when its root's opacity and pointerEvents change (101 updates a toggle); the cause is not explained.",
    "Hermes' tracker of unhandled rejections reports from a timer and not at the rejection, so the soak waits 2.3 s before reading the count and its control is a TypeError."
  ],
  "decisions": {
    "mountOrHide": "unmount by default; hide only a panel of about 100 nodes or more that is opened often on the click the player waits for, and at most one or two at a time, with pointerEvents none on its root and a body that does not depend on whether it is shown",
    "appliedToTheHud": false,
    "note": "a recommendation for V05-05, which owns consumers/civ-lite/; this slice does not change it"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Local macOS arm64 evidence, headless only; hosted CI is pending.",
    "The events are synthetic, delivered through Input.parse_input_event: no hardware pointer, no real touch screen, no iPhone, no mobile export.",
    "One machine under load from other agents (the load average is recorded before and after each command): the durations vary by tens of percent from one run to the next, and are the CPU cost of work on a loop nothing paces, not frame times.",
    "The 101 node updates of a hide toggle are not explained, and whether a cheaper way to hide a panel exists is open.",
    "The recommendation that the HUD layer of the V05-05 scene be PROCESS_MODE_ALWAYS (consumers/civ-lite/main.tscn's HUDLayer sets none) is not applied: another owner.",
    "The resident memory is judged loosely (48 MiB between the medians of the halves, within a run band of 34 to 137 MB over the runs made) and the heap rule judges the JavaScript heap only: a native leak under about 1 MiB a turn is not seen by either.",
    "The HUD is a fixture and the player one fixed rule over a game that stops changing after turn 14; the turno and congelado criteria of V05-06 stay open."
  ],
